t={'id':'illinois-osa-sbrt-dc-homing-hydrogel','title':'SBRT plus dendritic-cell homing hydrogel for canine appendicular osteosarcoma','center':'University of Illinois Veterinary Teaching Hospital','country':'USA','state':'Illinois','species':'Dog','cancers':['Osteosarcoma'],'status':'Currently listed as a funded clinical trial on the Illinois master roster','url':url,'contacts':'Rebecca Kamerer, Clinical Trials Coordinator — rmoss81@illinois.edu; 217-300-6453. Appointments: 217-333-5300.','funding':'Fully funded after eligibility: CT, biopsy, three-day SBRT, hydrogel injection, study recheck exams and bloodwork. Owners pay the initial consultation (approximately $250), eligibility diagnostics, pain medication and unrelated care.','funding_status':'Fully funded after screening','requires':{'confirmed':True,'active_treatment_target':True,'appendicular_location':True,'no_metastasis':True,'min_age_years_exclusive':1,'min_weight_kg':5,'planned_radiation':True,'anesthesia_candidate':True,'steroid_washout_days':14},'excludes':{'prior_chemo':True,'prior_local_radiation':True,'prior_immunotherapy':True,'current_steroids':True,'immunosuppressive':True},'notes':'Individual current official PDF read in full October 14, 2026. Dogs strictly older than one year, at least 5 kg, with histologic or cytologic alkaline-phosphatase-positive appendicular osteosarcoma; no chest/abdominal metastasis, no previous chemotherapy, radiation or immunotherapy. No Apoquel, topical/systemic steroids or immune modulators within 14 days. Adequate organ function for sedation; significant preexisting renal/hepatic/cardiac disease and autoimmune history exclude entry. Eligibility diagnostics within 14 days. CT and tumor biopsy under anesthesia, SBRT on three consecutive days, then peritumoral DC-homing hydrogel immediately after the third fraction. Blood sampling four days later and weekly follow-up for five weeks; other traditional treatments may follow completion. This is distinct from the JEN-101/radiation protocol requiring amputation.','intervention':'Three consecutive days of SBRT followed by local dendritic-cell homing hydrogel; weekly follow-up for five weeks','sites':[{'hospital':'University of Illinois Veterinary Teaching Hospital','name':'University of Illinois Veterinary Teaching Hospital','city':'Urbana','state':'IL'}],'verified':'2026-10-14','study_type':'treatment','available_for_matching':True,'status_confidence':'confirmed_current','owner_prescreen_required':True,'treatment_approaches':['radiation_innovation','immunotherapy'],'special_requirement':'Strictly age >1 year and weight ≥5 kg; nonmetastatic appendicular OSA. No prior radiation, chemo or immunotherapy; 14-day washout for Apoquel/steroids/immune modulators. Team must confirm anesthetic fitness, organ disease, autoimmune history and staging. Amputation is not a mandatory part of this separate SBRT/hydrogel protocol.'}
